Checking noted deviations in measurement of total RNA

Deviations include:
- Samples that where noted as "small" during measurement - meaning less than 1.7ul was pipetted on the uDrop plate
- Samples marked with "NS" (no sample)
- Samples where the absorbance curved of one of the four replicates deviated from the others

Rules for exclusion
- All samples marked "NS" will be excluded
- Samples with a deviating absorbance curve in addition to clear deviation in purity
- Samples marked as small and clearly deviating in purity/concentration?

